---
// Change the component name after migration, AboutWebmaster.astro, makes more sense
import Panel from "@components/primitives/Panel.astro";
---
<Panel
    as="section"
    class="about-webmaster"
    title="About the webmaster" 
>
    <div class="about-webmaster__body">
        <p>
            Hello, wanderer.<br />
            My name is <em>Atl</em>; it means
            <em>water</em> in Nahuatl. I’m a student. I’m interested in technology,
            programming, robotics, and math, and I also like coffee, rainy days, and books,
            especially science fiction, fantasy, and stories with magic in them. My first language
            is Spanish, and I’m learning English as a second language, so writing
            here is part of that process too. I live in a rainy place near the forest,
            in the mountains close to a volcano, with my two cats, <em>Tohru</em>
            and <em>Ragnar</em>. They will probably appear here from time to
            time. As for this website, I’m always moving things around and
            keeping it under maintenance. ( ´ ▽ ` )ﾉﾞ
        </p>
    </div>
</Panel>

<style>
    /* Scoped Panel heading override */
    .about-webmaster {
        padding: 0;
    }

    .about-webmaster > :global(.panel__heading) {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0.82rem var(--space-md);
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .about-webmaster__body {
        padding: 0.82rem var(--space-md);
    }
    /* Scoped Panel heading override */
</style>